# Cloudflare Pages — response headers
#
# ## Why this file exists
#
# `public/.htaccess` carries this site's entire security posture: 9 header
# directives, the Content-Security-Policy, HSTS, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy
# and Permissions-Policy. **Cloudflare Pages ignores `.htaccess` completely.** A
# build deployed to Pages without this file serves the site with *no* security
# headers at all — and fails silently, because nothing reports a missing header.
#
# The Apache file has a `verify:apache` harness that proves each header on a real
# server. This file is the Cloudflare equivalent of that same policy, kept in step
# by `verify-build-output.mjs`, which fails the build if `dist/_headers` is absent
# or has lost the CSP.
#
# ## ⚠️ One deliberate weakening, and why
#
# `.htaccess` picks one of **three CSP profiles per route** using
# `SetEnvIf Request_URI` — strict for editorial pages, relaxed for ad-bearing
# listings, article, and media for video pages. Cloudflare's `_headers` matches on
# **path patterns only, with no regular expressions**, so the article rule — which
# is "exactly three path segments, and the middle one is not `page`" — cannot be
# expressed at all.
#
# Rather than approximate it wrongly, this file sends the **union** of all four
# profiles on every route. That is measurably more permissive than the Apache
# configuration:
#
#   * pages that are currently `frame-src 'none'` may now frame YouTube, Facebook
#     and Google ad units;
#   * `'unsafe-inline'` is permitted in `script-src` everywhere.
#
# Every ad slot, embed and API the site actually calls still works, and the
# protections that matter most — no third-party script except Google's ad and
# video hosts, `frame-ancestors 'none'`, `object-src 'none'`, no `form-action`
# escape, `upgrade-insecure-requests` — are all retained.
#
# Restoring per-route strictness needs **Cloudflare Transform Rules** (or WAF
# custom rules), which *are* set from the dashboard and cannot be expressed in this
# file. That is the follow-up, not a gap to leave.
#
# ## Caching
#
# `.htaccess` marks `/_astro/*` and `/fonts/*` immutable (their filenames are
# content-hashed) and forces HTML to revalidate so a publish is visible as soon as
# the batch window closes.
#
# ⚠️ **`Cache-Control` is set ONLY on the hashed families, never on `/*`.** When
# more than one rule matches, Cloudflare **appends** the values instead of letting
# the more specific rule win. Setting it on both produced, on a hashed asset:
#
#     cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000, immutable
#
# which is self-contradictory — the asset is told to revalidate immediately *and*
# never to change for a year. Measured on the first live deploy (2026-10-09).
# Pages already sends `max-age=0, must-revalidate` for HTML on its own, so the
# `/*` rule is not needed to express that half; it was only ever creating the
# conflict. `verify-build-output.mjs` now asserts the two are never both set.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https://cms.shikkha24.com https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.gstatic.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://cms.shikkha24.com https://api.aladhan.com https://api.open-meteo.com https://ipwho.is https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.google.com https://*.doubleclick.net; media-src 'self' https://cms.shikkha24.com; frame-src https://*.googlesyndication.com https://*.doubleclick.net https://*.google.com https://googleads.g.doubleclick.net https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://www.youtube.com https://www.facebook.com https://web.facebook.com https://m.facebook.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
